{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>There is a way that seems straight</b> — who placed it before a man to engage in words of pleasantness?" "<b>and its end</b> — that he abandon it, he will find ways of death. And he said: 'ways,' because the causes of death are many. Another interpretation: that he go ways that will bring him to death."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:12.522683686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}